{"depth":"light","paper_type":"theory_or_simulation_compared_to_alma","paper_type_evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"Synthetic PV cuts are constructed from self-similar MHD DW solutions over a broad range of parameters."},{"loc":"abstract","quote":"Predictions for the "double-peak separation" method are tested on published ALMA observations of the HH212 rotating SO wind"}],"fields":["protoplanetary_disks","star_formation"],"question":{"value":"Which systematic biases affect the launch radius, magnetic lever arm and angular momentum flux of an MHD disk wind when inferred from apparent rotation signatures in ALMA-like PV diagrams, and do published HH212 ALMA data confirm the predictions?","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"We wish to identify systematic biases in retrieving the true launch zone, magnetic lever arm, and associated angular momentum flux of an MHD DW from apparent rotation signatures"}]},"targets":[{"name":"HH212","details":[{"loc":"4 Application to the edge-on rotating flow in HH212","quote":"we adopt for HH212 a systemic velocity of $V_{\rm sys}$ = 1.7 km s$^{-1}$(cite: 2014ApJ...786..114L) and a distance $d$ = 450 pc."}],"coordinates":"not stated","redshift_or_distance":"450 pc (inclination 87 deg)","distance_source":"adopted for consistency with Tabone et al. 2017; VLBI Orion B parallaxes suggest ~400 pc (Kounkel et al. 2017)"}],"alma_project_codes":[{"code":"2012.1.00997.S","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgements","quote":"This paper makes use of the ALMA 2012.1.00997.S and 2016.1.01475.S data (PI: C. Codella)."}]},{"code":"2016.1.01475.S","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgements","quote":"This paper makes use of the ALMA 2012.1.00997.S and 2016.1.01475.S data (PI: C. Codella)."}]}],"data_settings":[{"field":"angular_resolution","value":"HH212 SO data at 0.55" (~250 au), 0.15" (~65-70 au), 0.04" (18 au)","evidence":[{"loc":"4.1","quote":"SO blue/red channel maps of the base of the HH212 flow obtained at $0.55" \simeq$ 250 au resolution in ALMA Cycle 0 by (cite: 2015A&A...581A..85P)."}]}],"lines_targeted":[{"species":"SO","transition":"not stated","rest_frequency":"not stated","evidence":[{"loc":"4.2","quote":"through the disk atmosphere at $z \le$ 45 au, with an unprecedented resolution of 0.04$''$ = 18 au."}]}],"other_facilities":[],"external_data_from_literature":[{"what":{"value":"SO channel maps at 0.55" (Cycle 0) of HH212","evidence":[{"loc":"4.1","quote":"obtained at $0.55" \simeq$ 250 au resolution in ALMA Cycle 0 by (cite: 2015A&A...581A..85P)"}]},"citation":"(cite: 2015A&A...581A..85P)"},{"what":{"value":"SO PV cuts and apparent j ~30±15 au km/s at 0.04" resolution","evidence":[{"loc":"4.1","quote":"Their value $\simeq 30 \pm 15$  au km s$^{-1}$ remains remarkably similar to our results at 0.55$''$ and 0.15$''$."}]},"citation":"(cite: 2018ApJ...856...14L)"},{"what":{"value":"0.15" SO/SO2 data and MHD DW model for HH212 (L5W30, r_out=40 au)","evidence":[{"loc":"4.2","quote":"It was obtained with the MHD DW solution L5W30, $r_{\rm out}$= 40 au, $M_\star=0.2 M_{\odot}$, $i=87^{\circ}$"}]},"citation":"(cite: 2017A&A...607L...6T)"}],"simulations_or_models_as_data":[{"value":"Self-similar MHD disk wind solutions L13W36, L13W130, L5W30, L5W17 used to build synthetic PV cuts","evidence":[{"loc":"2 MHD disk-wind solutions","quote":"Four semi-analytical solutions of magneto-centrifugal MHD disk winds (hereafter MHD DW), of which three are new, were computed"}]}],"calibration":[],"imaging":[],"inherited":[{"what":{"value":"HH212 MHD DW model parameters, systemic velocity and distance","evidence":[{"loc":"4","quote":"For consistency with our previous modeling work in (cite: 2017A&A...607L...6T), we adopt for HH212 a systemic velocity"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: 2017A&A...607L...6T)"},{"what":{"value":"Self-similar MHD DW solution formalism","evidence":[{"loc":"2 MHD disk-wind solutions","quote":"developed and described by (cite: 1997A&A...319..340F; 2000A&A...353.1115C; 2000A&A...361.1178C), to which the reader is referred for more details"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: 1997A&A...319..340F; 2000A&A...353.1115C; 2000A&A...361.1178C)"}],"unstated_but_needed":["Radiative transfer/synthetic channel map code not named","Calibration and imaging of the reused ALMA data not described","Spectro-astrometry centroid fitting details (channel ranges, noise treatment)","Numerical solutions of the MHD DW ODEs not released"],"analysis_steps":[{"order":1,"goal":"Build synthetic PV cuts from MHD DW solutions","method":{"value":"Self-similar solutions scaled to physical units, power-law emissivity, convolved with Gaussian beam at 0.44 km/s sampling","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"a parametrized emissivity function is adopted with a a simple power law radial variation"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[{"value":"M*=0.1 Msun, r_in=0.25 au, r_out=8 au, i=87 deg, alpha=-2, beam 225 au, z_cut=225 au","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"$M_\star=0.1M_{\odot}$, $r_{\rm in}=0.25$ au, $r_{\rm out}=8$ au, $i=87^{\circ}$, $\alpha = -2$, and $\theta_b= 225$ au"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"Steady, axisymmetric, self-similar wind; optically thin","evidence":[{"loc":"4.2","quote":"our MHD DW model is probably too idealized (self-similar, steady, axisymmetric)"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}},{"order":2,"goal":"Estimate j_obs, r_obs, lambda_obs with three methods and compare with true values","method":{"value":"Double-peak separation, rotation curve and flow width methods; Anderson's relation solved for r_obs","evidence":[{"loc":"3.2","quote":"we will thus consider three methods used by observers to estimate the flow specific angular momentum from PV cuts at ALMA-like resolution"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Compared to true j_out, r_out, lambda_BP on outermost streamline","evidence":[]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Test predictions on HH212 ALMA data","method":{"value":"Spectro-astrometry of blue/red centroids in 0.55" channel maps; compare PV cuts and model at 250, 70, 18 au","evidence":[{"loc":"4.1","quote":"spatial shifts much smaller than the beam can still be detected by comparing centroid positions (the so-called “spectro-astrometry" technique)"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"d = 450 pc, Vsys = 1.7 km/s, M*=0.2 Msun","evidence":[]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Same model compared at three resolutions","evidence":[]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Angular momentum extraction fraction f_J","method":{"value":"Analytic f_J = lambda_BP [1 + ln(r_out/r_in)/(2 ln(1+f_M))]^-1 applied with f_M from SO mass flux and accretion rate","evidence":[{"loc":"4.3","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
\label{eq:fracj2}
f_J =  \lambda_{\rm BP} \times \left[ {1+ \frac{ \ln (r_{\rm out}/r_{\rm in}) }{2 \ln (1+f_M)} } \right]^{-1}.
\end{equation}$$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]}}],"software":[],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"HH212 spatial shift at z~70 au (0.55")","value":"0.06","uncertainty":"0.02","units":"arcsec","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"4.1","quote":"The shift amplitude at $z \simeq 70$ au is $\Delta r \simeq 0.06"\pm 0.02"$ (27 au)"}]},{"quantity":"HH212 apparent specific angular momentum","value":"27","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au km/s","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"4.1","quote":"the apparent specific angular momentum in both data sets is $j_{\rm obs}$$=(\Delta r/2)(\Delta V/2)\simeq$ 27 au km s$^{-1}$"}]},{"quantity":"HH212 r_obs from Anderson relation","value":"~1","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"4.2","quote":"Anderson's relation yields an estimated $r_{\rm obs}$$\simeq 1$ au."}]},{"quantity":"f_M,obs for HH212","value":"0.33-3.3","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"dimensionless","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"4.3","quote":"we infer an ejection to accretion ratio $f_{M,\rm obs}$ = $\dot{M}_{\rm DW}$/ $\dot{M}_{\rm in}$= 0.33 – 3.3"}]},{"quantity":"f_J,obs for HH212","value":"0.5-1.8","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"dimensionless","from_step":4,"evidence":[{"loc":"4.3","quote":"we obtain $f_{J,\rm obs}$ = 0.5 – 1.8"}]},{"quantity":"Flow-width method r_obs and lambda_obs (reference model, i=40)","value":"r_obs ~1.5 au, lambda_obs ~2","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"au; dimensionless","from_step":2,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.5","quote":"we obtain with Anderson's method $r_{\rm obs}$$\simeq 1.5$ au and $\lambda_{\rm obs}$$\simeq 2$"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"Magnetic lever arm from Anderson's formula is always a lower limit due to angular momentum in magnetic torsion","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The magnetic lever arm is always underestimated, due to invisible angular momentum stored as magnetic field torsion."}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"Double-peak separation recovers the true outer launch radius","experiment":"Synthetic PV cuts of self-similar MHD DWs with varied parameters","result":"r_obs is always a lower limit, independent of resolution, up to factor 10 off","finding":"Double-peak and flow-width methods underestimate r_out; rotation curve works when resolved","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The "double-peak separation" method and the "flow width" method provide only a lower limit to the true outer launch radius $r_{\rm out}$."}]},{"hypothesis":"HH212 SO wind follows predicted biases","experiment":"Compare PV peak separation at 250, 65 and 18 au resolution with the MHD DW model","result":"j_obs ~27-30 au km/s at all resolutions, r_obs ~1 au vs r_out ~40 au","finding":"ALMA data confirm the predicted biases and large r_out","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"ALMA data of HH212 confirm our predicted biases for the "double-peak separation" method"}]},{"hypothesis":"The HH212 MHD DW can sustain disk accretion","experiment":"Apply analytic f_J with observed f_M","result":"f_J = 0.5-1.8","finding":"Enough angular momentum is extracted to sustain accretion","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"The MHD DW candidate in HH212 extracts enough angular momentum to sustain steady accretion through the whole disk at the current observed rate."}]}],"reasoning":[],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[{"value":"Swept-up shell driven by an X-wind, or bowshock-shocked disk wind, cannot be ruled out","evidence":[{"loc":"4.2","quote":"Nevertheless, our proposed interpretation in terms of MHD DW is not unique."}]}],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Analysis is limited to self-similar steady axisymmetric models; biases may differ for other geometries","evidence":[{"loc":"5 Conclusions","quote":"While our analysis strictly pertains only to self-similar models, we expect similar biases to occur in more general geometries"}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["ALMA data are not reprocessed; relies on published measurements","Emissivity is a parametrized power law, not chemistry","Distance uncertainty (400 vs 450 pc)"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"ALMA projects 2012.1.00997.S and 2016.1.01475.S acknowledged","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgements","quote":"This paper makes use of the ALMA 2012.1.00997.S and 2016.1.01475.S data (PI: C. Codella)."}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["MHD DW solution numerical profiles","Synthetic imaging code","Calibrated HH212 images"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"tens of GB if archival data re-reduced","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"Theory dominates; analytic parts reproducible but the model solutions and imaging pipeline are not provided.","rediscovery_candidate":false,"rediscovery_reason":"Main results rely on custom MHD solutions and published, not reprocessed, ALMA products.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: 2003ApJ...590L.107A)","why":"Anderson's relation for launch radius"},{"citation":"(cite: 1997A&A...319..340F)","why":"Self-similar MHD disk wind formalism"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"(cite: 2017A&A...607L...6T)","why":"Original HH212 MHD DW model"},{"citation":"(cite: 2018ApJ...856...14L)","why":"0.04" SO observations of HH212"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":[]}
